<title>GERMANY: Holzmann - 96 financials clearly improved.</title>
<headline>Holzmann - 96 financials clearly improved.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>German construction company Philipp Holzmann AG said on Tuesday that its financial situation had clearly improved in 1996 and that it aimed to return its loss-making units to profit by 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;Holzmann will continue its determined restructuring programme in 1997,&quot; the group said in a statement.</p>
<p>The group said its liquid assets and securities rose to 2.6 billion marks ($1.5 billion) from 1.7 billion marks in 1996. Earlier, Holzmann said group construction output rose to 14.06 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.703 German Marks)</p>
